    "notes": "If display auto-off is disabled in the app, this should work out of the box.\n\nIf display auto-off is enabled, then: When device is off, a single click of the power button will turn it on. When device is on, all actions need a button press (any button press) to make the device receptive, then the real button press within 5 seconds. Repeats weren't added to the commands - if they had been, in a 5 second window the first 'Speed Up' registered would step the fan 1 level, the next would step it up 2 levels. I've made it all work for me by creating a script that presses the 'Mode'  button then delays 150 milliseconds before sending the button I actually want to trigger. (Changing between auto and manual modes has minimal impacts.)",
